{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01K5C6iqpPX6JUGdyRbzTwAA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is a grounded bullet-claim summary of the planning trio session.\n\n## foreman-handoff-dashboard\n\n**Source:** `docs/foreman-handoff-dashboard/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md` â€” \"Aurora Dashboard â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\"\n\n### North Star & guardrails\n- The goal is a **locally-served, read-only web dashboard** giving John one morning view of Aurora's nightly fleet: results + health at a glance + a visual catalog explorer, so he never reads raw JSON/markdown.\n- It is **strictly read-only** against `kb/aurora.db` (`mode=ro`) and `reports/`; never writes the KB/library/reports, never reads `.env`, and binds to `127.0.0.1:5001`.\n- It is **additive only** â€” new code under `dashboard/`, a root launcher `aurora_dashboard.py`, and `tests/test_dashboard_*.py`; no edits to existing Aurora modules and no migrations.\n- Architecture is a **self-contained blueprint-factory + Flask-agnostic data layer** so it can later mount as an Anchor tab; the data layer never imports Flask and the blueprint never imports orchestrator/sweep code.\n- Process discipline: the **working tree is production** â€” every wave ends clean and committed; **no test weakening**, the count may only rise. Test command: `python -m pytest tests/ -k dashboard -q`.\n- Stage-0 lock and gap decisions live in `STAGE0-FRAMING.md`; the data contract is grounded in `kb/schema.sql` and live `reports/` surfaces as of 2026-06-11; **waves run in series**, and cited row counts are drifting snapshots (every query resolves its set by rule).\n\n### Wave plan (6 waves, sequential)\n- **Wave 1 â€” Read-only scaffold + data layer + serving shell:** stands up the `dashboard/` package, a proven read-only DB handle (`ro_connect` with `mode=ro` + `PRAGMA query_only=ON` + a write-guard), freshness/fingerprint, the app/blueprint factory, and a live HTML shell with a freshness header and fingerprint poll. Routes: `/api/health`, `/api/fingerprint`, `/api/state`. Done-when proves write-rejection, embeddability on a bare Flask app, and soft-fail on missing KB/reports.\n- **Wave 2 â€” Morning glance panel:** `reports.py` readers parse `reports/morning/latest_summary.json` (productivity index, status, window, sample_size, MTD costs, finds/finds_new, top_finds, noise_audit, badges), the briefing note, and latest weekly. `/api/morning` composes them; the panel renders top-find cards, an adoption line that **always shows window + sample_size (never a bare %)**, a cost rollup with MTD, and the briefing note. All readers fail soft.\n- **Wave 3 â€” Errors/health panel (signals + in-page detail, G3):** `health.py` reads latest `runs` row per sweep (status + `critic_c` degrade flag), noise_audit categories with offending rows, backfill audits, recent rejects, and a **path-allowlisted** `sweep_log_tail`. `/api/health` + `/api/health/detail?signal=` let each non-zero signal expand inline. Explicitly defends the **path-traversal/secret-exposure trap** (refuses `../../.env` / absolute paths).\n- **Wave 4 â€” \"What was new\" per-sweep results browser:** `list_sweep_dates(kind)` + `read_sweep(kind, date)` (allowlisted to `reports/<kind>/`); `/api/sweeps` + `/api/sweep/<kind>/<date>`; a kindÃ—date selector defaulting to latest, reachable from the morning finds-new links. Refuses traversal kinds/dates; missing date â†’ soft empty.\n- **Wave 5 â€” Catalog taxonomy map (G1 v1):** `catalog.py` builds `taxonomy_map()` over non-retired `artifacts` LEFT JOIN `embeddings` grouped by `kind Ã— domain_path` (NULL â†’ \"unclassified\"), aggregating count + mean `interest_score` + a dead-link/stars overlay from `link_health`; `artifacts_in(kind, domain_path)` returns wedge artifacts (name, taste why, stars, usage from `hh_events`, dead-flag, URL). `map.js` reuses the `library/_map.html` D3 sunburst/icicle idiom with click-to-filter.\n- **Wave 6 â€” Polish, embeddability proof, docs:** global aggregated \"as of\" header, audited empty/error states, `DASHBOARD.md` (run + **exact Anchor-tab mount steps**), an integration test mounting the blueprint on a second bare Flask app exercising **every** `/api/*` route, a **deferred-work note** for a force-directed knowledge-graph (sources: shared `domain_path`, `github_network_parent`, `prov_edges`, `hh_events`), and a live read-only smoke confirming all panels render with KB/reports mtimes unchanged.\n\n### Cross-cutting \"subtle traps\" the plan calls out\n- **Hard constraint #1 â€” read-only guarantee:** proven by a write-rejection test (W1) and an end-to-end mtime-unchanged smoke (W6).\n- **Hard constraint #2 â€” path-traversal/secret exposure:** allowlist tests in W3 and W4 (refuse `..`/absolute/`.env`).\n- **PM2 â€” Anchor-tab boundary/coupling trap:** embeddability proven by mounting the blueprint on a bare Flask app with no Aurora imports (W1) and across all routes (W6).\n- **Thin-window trap (inherited from the quality build):** adoption/productivity must always be labeled with window + sample_size (W2).\n\nNote: the file globs show `dashboard/web/static/` assets and `tests/test_dashboard_*.py` already exist in the tree, so implementation against this plan appears to be at least partly underway â€” consistent with the memory index note that a read-only Flask dashboard shipped 2026-06-11."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7212,"cache_read_input_tokens":33775,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7212},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e4048b5-6f55-482d-8b60-0338612926b6","uuid":"d8bc638c-90cc-477a-bda2-234841ea1df6","request_id":"req_011CcKGzS9xDVv4UM3KwRg8g"}
